§ `Which years the deposited text covers`

#ASSERT `What is the tax-free threshold` EQUALS 18200
#ASSERT NOT `Does the deposited text give rates for my year` 2023
#ASSERT `Does the deposited text give rates for my year` 2024

#ASSERT `Which resident table applies to my year` 2025 EQUALS `the table for 2024-25 or 2025-26`
#ASSERT `Which resident table applies to my year` 2026 EQUALS `the table for 2026-27`
#ASSERT `Which resident table applies to my year` 2033 EQUALS `the table for 2027-28 or a later year`

§ `s 3 resident taxpayer; s 3A working holiday maker; ss 18, 20 threshold`

#ASSERT NOT `Am I a resident taxpayer` TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT `Am I a resident taxpayer` TRUE TRUE

#ASSERT `Was I a working holiday maker` `a work bridging visa awaiting a 417 or 462 decision, after a 417 or 462`
#ASSERT NOT `Was I a working holiday maker` `another visa, or none`

#ASSERT `What is my working holiday taxable income` 32000 2000 EQUALS 30000

#ASSERT `Is there a part-year residency period for me` TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `Is there a part-year residency period for me` TRUE TRUE

#ASSERT `What tax-free threshold do I get` FALSE FALSE FALSE 0 EQUALS 0
#ASSERT `What tax-free threshold do I get` TRUE TRUE FALSE 13650 EQUALS 13650
#ASSERT `What tax-free threshold do I get` TRUE TRUE TRUE 13650 EQUALS 18200

§ `Schedule 7 -- the lives`

-- c045: 2023-24 is not in the deposited text. For comparison, the 2024-25 table on $27,500: 9,300 x 16% = 1,488.
-- c048: (45,000 - 18,200) x 16% = 4,288 plus (71,500 - 45,000) x 30% = 7,950: 12,238, not the scenario's 12,842.
-- k043 (ITAA cross-check): (31,000 - 18,200) x 14% = 1,792.
#ASSERT `How much tax is on my taxable income` `Chloe, 2023-24 return (c045)` EQUALS `Not in the deposited text`
